# These artefacts are COMPARED BYTE FOR BYTE by base/meta/renders.py, so git may
# not rewrite their line endings on checkout. Without this, `git add` warns "LF
# will be replaced by CRLF", a Windows desk and a Linux desk check out different
# bytes for the same baseline, and the gate's verdict depends on which machine
# ran it rather than on the library.
#
# renders.py also normalises CRLF to LF when it READS an artefact, so the gate
# survives a checkout that ignored this file. Both halves are deliberate: the
# attribute keeps the stored bytes stable, and the normalisation keeps the gate
# honest if they are not.
*.out text eol=lf
MANIFEST.tsv text eol=lf
EXPECTED-DIFFS.tsv text eol=lf
